{#
  The fields of ONE signer (issue #989, lot D; ARCHITECTURE.md §8.125):
  what the signature dialog (partials/signature_dialog.html.twig) shows in
  its body, and what a page signing a document in the page itself — not
  in a dialog — renders once per signer inside its own form. Two signers
  on one document, the renter as a witness and the manager with the
  account's signature, are two includes with two prefixes in one form:

      <form method="post" action="…" enctype="multipart/form-data"
            data-signature-form data-signature-inline-form>
          {{ csrf_field()|raw }}
          {% include 'partials/signature_fields.html.twig' with {
              id: 'inventory-renter', name_prefix: 'renter_', witness: true,
          } only %}
          {% include 'partials/signature_fields.html.twig' with {
              id: 'inventory-manager', has_stored_signature: true,
              manage_return: '/mes-locations/…',
          } only %}
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">…</button>
      </form>

  `name_prefix` (default '', which is the dialog's) goes in front of every
  field name — `signature_source`, `signature_data`, `signature_file`,
  `remember_signature`, `signer_name` —, so that one signer's drawing never
  lands in the other's field; the server reads it back with the same
  prefix (SignatureSubmission::fromRequest(), PersonalSignatureService::
  witnessFromRequest()), which accepts lowercase letters followed by one
  underscore and nothing else. `id` prefixes the element ids, and must
  differ between the two includes of one page.

  The modes are the dialog's — stored (`has_stored_signature`), new (with
  `allow_import` and `allow_remember`, both default true), witness
  (`witness: true`) —, and so is `consequence`, the module's sentence. The
  container, `[data-signature-field]`, is what signature-pad.js wires: one
  pad and one hidden field each, so two of them in one form draw apart.
  The page loads signature-pad.js then signature-dialog.js, which empties
  every container of a form once it is sent and on a page restored from
  the back-forward cache, and fetches the stored signature's preview into
  `[data-signature-preview]` — never written into this page, which may be
  cached (decision Q5).

  Never an account id among the fields: whose signature it is, is the
  session's to say (Core\Signature\SignatureSubmission).
#}
{% set name_prefix = name_prefix|default('') %}
{% set witness = witness|default(false) %}
{% set stored = not witness and has_stored_signature|default(false) %}
{% set allow_import = not witness and (allow_import is defined ? allow_import : true) %}
{% set allow_remember = not witness and (allow_remember is defined ? allow_remember : true) %}
{% set consequence = consequence|default('') %}
{% set manage_return = manage_return|default('') %}
<div data-signature-field data-signature-mode="{{ witness ? 'witness' : (stored ? 'stored' : 'new') }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="{{ name_prefix }}signature_source" value="{{ stored ? 'stored' : 'new' }}">

    {% if stored %}
        <p>Ce document sera signé avec la signature enregistrée dans votre compte. Vérifiez son contenu avant de confirmer.</p>
        {% if consequence %}<p>{{ consequence }}</p>{% endif %}
        {# Filled by signature-dialog.js when the dialog opens (or the page shows a form of its own), emptied when it closes. #}
        <div class="border rounded bg-white p-2 mb-2 text-center" data-signature-preview
             style="min-height: 4rem;"></div>
        <p class="small mb-0">
            <a href="/account/signature{{ manage_return ? '?retour=' ~ manage_return|url_encode : '' }}">Gérer ma signature</a>
        </p>
    {% else %}
        {% if consequence %}<p>{{ consequence }}</p>{% endif %}
        {% if witness %}
            <div class="mb-3">
                <label class="form-label" for="{{ id }}-signer-name">Nom de la personne qui signe</label>
                <input type="text" class="form-control" id="{{ id }}-signer-name" name="{{ name_prefix }}signer_name"
                       maxlength="120" required autocomplete="off">
            </div>
        {% endif %}
        <input type="hidden" name="{{ name_prefix }}signature_data" value="">

        <p class="form-label mb-1" id="{{ id }}-pad-label">{{ witness ? 'Signature' : 'Tracez votre signature' }}</p>
        {#
          Traced with a pointer, so no role of its own: « img »
          would tell assistive technology there is nothing to do
          here. Without a pointer, the import below is the way in.
        #}
        <canvas data-signature-pad width="900" height="300"
                aria-labelledby="{{ id }}-pad-label"
                class="border rounded bg-white w-100 d-block" style="aspect-ratio: 3 / 1;"></canvas>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary mt-2" data-signature-clear>Effacer</button>
        {% if witness %}
            <p class="form-text mb-0">La signature est ajoutée à ce document seulement : elle n'est gardée nulle part ailleurs, et le cadre est effacé dès que vous signez ou annulez.</p>
        {% endif %}

        {% if allow_import %}
            <div class="mt-3">
                <label class="form-label" for="{{ id }}-file">Ou importez une image de votre signature</label>
                <input type="file" class="form-control" id="{{ id }}-file" name="{{ name_prefix }}signature_file"
                       accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp" aria-describedby="{{ id }}-file-help">
                <p class="form-text" id="{{ id }}-file-help">PNG, JPEG ou WebP, 5 Mo au plus.</p>
            </div>
        {% endif %}

        {% if allow_remember %}
            <div class="form-check mt-3">
                <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" name="{{ name_prefix }}remember_signature" value="1"
                       id="{{ id }}-remember" aria-describedby="{{ id }}-remember-help">
                <label class="form-check-label" for="{{ id }}-remember">Mémoriser ma signature dans mon compte pour une utilisation future</label>
                <p class="form-text mb-0" id="{{ id }}-remember-help">
                    Sans cette case, la signature sert à ce document seulement et n'est pas gardée.
                </p>
            </div>
        {% endif %}

        <p class="text-danger small mt-2 mb-0" data-signature-missing hidden role="alert">
            {{ allow_import ? "Tracez votre signature ou importez-en l'image." : 'Tracez la signature dans le cadre.' }}
        </p>
    {% endif %}
</div>
